SPU DMA: map the SPU thread local-store window (0xF0000000 + spu_num * 0x100000).

lv2 maps each SPU thread's local store into the effective-address space at SYS_SPU_THREAD_BASE_LOW + spu_num *
SYS_SPU_THREAD_OFFSET. mfc_do_transfer treated those addresses as guest memory, so a GET there returned zeros.
Resistance 3's collision job gathers 16-byte chunk records (collision mesh EA pairs) out of SPU 0's local store with
GETs from 0xF0007400; with zeros it tested every query against the same empty chunk, every ground probe missed, and
the player fell through the level the moment gameplay started.

GETs and PUTs in the window now copy between local stores. The peer is resolved within the issuing context's SPURS
instance: the SPU's own number reaches itself, another number reaches the policy context that entered that SPU
last. Plain SPU thread groups and the problem-state area above 0x40000 are not mapped yet (TODO in spu_dma.h).
New test runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_thread_ls_dma.c (also run by the macOS and Linux workflows).
test_mfc_resume_elements does not link spurs_policy.c: it stubs spu_thread_ls_peer (no peer).

Upstream: not proposed yet.
